<Layout title="Research">
  <h1>Research</h1>
  <p>
    I study how traumatic brain injury (TBI) affects the mechanics of the brain, using medical
    imaging and computation. At WashU, my work spans magnetic resonance elastography (MRE),
    diffusion tensor imaging (DTI), machine learning and metamaterial manufacturing. As an
    undergraduate at the University of Utah, I worked on how cerebral blood vessels soften after
    overstretch.
  </p>

  <h2>Publications</h2>
